# DE FACTO ONE-PARTY STATES #

A  [LINK: (de facto) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_facto]  one-party system is one that, while not officially linking a single political party to governmental power, utilizes some means of political manipulation to ensure only one party stays in power. [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-party_state#cite_note-24]  Many different countries have been claimed to be de facto one-party states, with differing levels of agreement between scholars, although most agree that the African continent is marked by this political system. [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-party_state#cite_note-25]  [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-party_state#cite_note-26]  [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-party_state#cite_note-27]  Below are just a few examples of governments that have been claimed to have single party rule due to political manipulation.


